{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 9.025,
   "text": "I work nights at a sleep clinic, watching strangers sleep on six small screens."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 9.625,
   "end": 12.612,
   "text": "The tech who trained me left one rule."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 13.212,
   "end": 19.569,
   "text": "If a patient ever sits up and stares into the camera... don't go in. Don't use the intercom. Just wait."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 20.369,
   "end": 23.463,
   "text": "For two months, all I saw was snoring."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 24.163,
   "end": 28.024,
   "text": "Then, at three a.m., the man in room six sat up."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 29.024,
   "end": 32.971,
   "text": "Slowly. Like something was lifting him by the collar."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 33.771,
   "end": 37.888,
   "text": "He turned to the camera, and he didn't blink. His lips were moving."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 38.588,
   "end": 41.105,
   "text": "I turned up the room audio."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 43.305,
   "end": 46.505,
   "text": "He was counting down. Five... four..."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 47.705,
   "end": 51.951,
   "text": "Room five sat up. Then room four. Then three. Then two."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 52.751,
   "end": 56.249,
   "text": "All of them, staring at me. All of them counting."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 57.249,
   "end": 61.26,
   "text": "I kept my hands flat on the desk, and I didn't breathe."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start": 62.66,
   "end": 63.339,
   "text": "One."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start": 65.939,
   "end": 69.886,
   "text": "That's when I remembered. There are only five patient rooms."
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start": 70.686,
   "end": 76.019,
   "text": "Screen one is the camera above my desk... and on it, I wasn't sitting alone."
  }
 ],
